WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:15.579
"I see the Valentine's Day cards," Mom said.

2
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.743
The Carter family was at the store.

3
00:00:18.744 --> 00:00:22.010
They were shopping for cards.

4
00:00:22.011 --> 00:00:26.661
Everything was pink or red.

5
00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:29.948
Hearts were everywhere.

6
00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:36.762
Harry groaned. "Valentine's Day is so dumb."

7
00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:41.859
"Oh, come on, Harry." Emmy giggled.

8
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.643
"Don't you have a valentine?"

9
00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:54.429
"No!" Harry made a face. "Gross!"

10
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.581
Most cards came with stickers or candy.

11
00:00:58.582 --> 00:01:03.526
Oliver found some with gel pens.

12
00:01:03.527 --> 00:01:06.240
Mom shook her head.

13
00:01:06.241 --> 00:01:12.293
"Those are too expensive."

14
00:01:12.294 --> 00:01:16.500
"Did you find any cards, Harry?" Dad asked.

15
00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:20.151
"No," Harry said.

16
00:01:20.152 --> 00:01:24.264
"All these cards have goofy hearts."

17
00:01:24.265 --> 00:01:27.782
Emmy picked out one big card.

18
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:31.451
"Who's that for?" Oliver asked.

19
00:01:31.452 --> 00:01:37.320
Emmy blushed. "I'm not telling you."

20
00:01:37.321 --> 00:01:40.775
Harry found cards with superheroes.

21
00:01:40.776 --> 00:01:42.877
"Even these have dumb hearts.

22
00:01:42.878 --> 00:01:46.242
But I guess they're okay."

23
00:01:46.243 --> 00:01:50.135
Finally it was Valentine's Day.

24
00:01:50.136 --> 00:01:55.244
"Valentine's Day is so dumb," Harry grumbled.

25
00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:57.258
Mom smiled.

26
00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:02.833
"Enjoy your class party," she said.

27
00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.793
Later Harry came home.

28
00:02:05.794 --> 00:02:10.882
He had a bag of valentines from his friends.

29
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:14.583
"How was the party?" Mom asked.

30
00:02:14.584 --> 00:02:19.126
"Great!" Harry said.

31
00:02:19.127 --> 00:02:22.068
"Really?" Mom said.

32
00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:25.549
"I thought you didn't like Valentine's Day."

33
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:29.580
Then she saw a big card in Harry's hand.

34
00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:32.819
Harry quickly hid it behind him.

35
00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.323
He grinned.

36
00:02:35.324 --> 00:02:40.724
"I think I like Valentine's Day after all!"
